TYPES.md §3.3, §5.1, §1, DECISIONS 333: a misspelled field in a record check whose other operand is context-dependent too (`weigth < 5`, `weigth == none`, `weigth + 1 > 5`, `-weigth < 5`, `(weigth) >= 0`) is found by no step of the lookup order (no expected type gives step 1 anything to look in), so it is E2102 with the field as the hint, not E3008; its operand takes the error type and the comparison reports nothing more. Two unknown names are one finding each (`Mon == Tue`). With a typed other operand (`weight < weigth`) it was already E2102. Only literals stay E3008 (E3008_5).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Box {
  weight: Int
  check light: weigth < 5 else "too heavy"
  check set: weigth == none else "unset"
  check sum: weigth + 1 > 5 else "too light"
  check neg: -weigth < 5 else "negative"
  check paren: (weigth) >= 0 else "negative"
  check typed: weight < weigth else "typed"
  check days: Mon == Tue else "days"
  check both: weigth > 0 and weight < 5 else "both"
}
